# Chaos: every spell picker sorted by level then name, with a working "Only show learned spells" box (Lua only;
# applies after 0001-0056).
# Pickers: the helper's Assign Healing / Attack Spell (assignSpell), Select Attack Spell (assignSpellForMagicShooter),
# Assign Training / Haste / Cure Paralyze Spell (assignTrainingSpell), the action bar's Assign Spell and the custom
# hotkeys' Assign Spell. Each one called ChaosSpellCore.setupPicker (overlay game_spellbook, spellbook_core.lua) where
# it sorted its rows by name: rows by level then name, rows above the character's level (or not learned) dimmed, the
# box and the search filter together, the remembered box state (g_settings chaosPickerLearnedOnly), and the empty
# preview at the top of the window says what to do.
# Root cause of the dead box: the helper forced it on and disabled it, and no picker read it (no onCheckChange).
# "Learned" is the Spellbook's rule (vocation, level, magic level, the server's learned list); the client's own spell
# list packet cannot tell, since the base server sends every spell id in it.
# Without the overlay module the pickers keep their old alphabetical order.
